diff --git a/docs/deployment-aws.md b/docs/deployment-aws.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5831b77
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment-aws.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Deployment design (AWS)
+
+How the local `docker-compose` topology maps onto AWS for a production-style
+deployment. This is the design for the report's "Deployment Flow" section; it
+describes the target architecture rather than a provisioned environment.
+
+## Local → AWS mapping
+
+| Local (docker-compose) | AWS service |
+| --- | --- |
+| `postgres` container | **Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL** (Multi-AZ) |
+| `redis` container | **Amazon ElastiCache for Redis** |
+| `kafka` container | **Amazon MSK** (Managed Streaming for Kafka) |
+| service containers | **Amazon ECS (Fargate)** tasks, or EC2 behind an ASG |
+| `api-gateway` | ECS service behind an **Application Load Balancer** |
+| images | **Amazon ECR** |
+
+## Network (VPC)
+
+- One **VPC** spanning **two Availability Zones** for high availability.
+- **Public subnets**: the Application Load Balancer only.
+- **Private subnets**: all service tasks (user, product, order, gateway), plus
+  RDS, ElastiCache and MSK. Nothing data-tier is publicly reachable.
+- **NAT Gateway** in a public subnet for private-subnet outbound (pulling images,
+  patching).
+
+## Security groups (least privilege)
+
+| From | To | Port |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Internet | ALB | 80 / 443 |
+| ALB | api-gateway tasks | 8080 |
+| api-gateway | user/product/order tasks | 8081 / 9090 / 9091 |
+| product/order tasks | user-service task | 8081 (token validation) |
+| order-service task | product-service task | 9090 (price lookup) |
+| service tasks | RDS | 5432 |
+| product-service task | ElastiCache | 6379 |
+| service tasks | MSK | 9092 |
+
+The database, cache and broker security groups accept traffic **only** from the
+service security group — never from the internet.
+
+## Configuration & secrets
+
+- Non-secret config via ECS task definition environment variables
+  (`SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=prod`, service URLs, broker endpoints).
+- Secrets (`JWT_SECRET`, DB credentials) in **AWS Secrets Manager** / SSM
+  Parameter Store, injected into tasks at runtime — never baked into images.
+
+## CI/CD (outline)
+
+1. Build & test on push (the Maven multi-module build).
+2. Build one image per service, tag with the commit SHA, push to **ECR**.
+3. Update the ECS service to the new task definition (rolling deployment with
+   health checks; roll back automatically on failed health checks).
+
+## Scaling & resilience
+
+- Each service scales independently via an ECS **service auto-scaling** policy
+  (target CPU / request count).
+- RDS Multi-AZ for failover; ElastiCache replication group; MSK across AZs.
+- Statelessness: services hold no session state in memory (JWT + DB + Redis),
+  so any task can serve any request — horizontal scaling is safe.
+
+## Diagram
+
+See the architecture diagram in the report (draw.io). Tiers top to bottom:
+Internet → ALB (public subnets) → API Gateway → {user, product, order} services
+(private subnets) → {RDS, ElastiCache, MSK} (private subnets).
